-- title:
--   Base change along Λ → k factors through Λ/I
-- statement:
--   Let $\Lambda$ be a commutative ring, $I \subseteq \Lambda$ an ideal, and $k$ a commutative ring carrying both a $\Lambda$-algebra structure and a $(\Lambda/I)$-algebra structure, assumed compatible in the sense that $\Lambda \to \Lambda/I \to k$ is the structure map $\Lambda \to k$ (a scalar-tower hypothesis for $\Lambda$, $\Lambda/I$, $k$). Let $A$ be a further commutative $\Lambda$-algebra. The assertion is that the type of $k$-algebra isomorphisms
--   $$k \otimes_{\Lambda} A \;\simeq\; k \otimes_{\Lambda/I} \bigl(A / I^{e}\bigr),$$
--   where $I^{e} = I\,A$ denotes the image ideal of $I$ under $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ \Lambda\ A$ (the ideal of $A$ generated by the image of $I$), is nonempty. Thus the base change of $A$ to $k$ may be computed over $\Lambda/I$ from the fibre $A/IA$. The statement is an existence assertion ($\mathtt{Nonempty}$) about an isomorphism, not a designated isomorphism; no particular map is named, and no finiteness, flatness or Noetherian hypothesis is imposed.
--
--   This is the standard compatibility of base change with passage to a fibre: $(\Lambda/I) \otimes_\Lambda A \cong A/IA$ combined with associativity of tensor products. It is used, for a field $k$ of residue characteristic, to replace $k \otimes_\Lambda A$ by $k \otimes_{\Lambda/I}(A/IA)$; it is cited in the computation of the Krull dimension of such a localised base change in [`IsIntegrallyClosed.ringKrullDim_localization_tensor_eq_one_of_irreducible`](thm.html#IsIntegrallyClosed.ringKrullDim_localization_tensor_eq_one_of_irreducible).
